# portfolio — master rule

The single always-applied rule that governs both the project and how the
assistant should work in this repo. Project overview, hard conventions, the
*clarification protocol*, and the *chat interaction guidelines* all live here.

## Project overview

A personal portfolio site built with **Gatsby**, **TypeScript**, and
**Tailwind CSS**. Statically built and deployed to **GitHub Pages**. There is no
backend, database, or server — all content is static and rendered at build time.

This repo is a **learning-oriented boilerplate**: `src/` ships with a
`README.md` in each subfolder describing what to build, but no implementation
files yet. The READMEs are canonical guidance — follow them when scaffolding.

## Tech stack

| Concern | Choice |
|---|---|
| Framework | Gatsby 5 (file-based routing, `Head` API, SSR + static build) |
| Language | TypeScript 5 (strict) |
| UI | React 18 |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS 3 + PostCSS, custom "Bold & Playful Paper" theme |
| Theme | Dark/light via React context (`localStorage` + system preference) |
| Deploy | GitHub Actions → GitHub Pages (`gh-pages` branch) |

## Source layout

```
src/
  types/        → shared TypeScript shapes (Project, Role, SkillGroup, Accent)
  data/         → static portfolio content as typed exports (no JSX)
  styles/       → global.css: Tailwind layers + design tokens (CSS vars)
  context/      → ThemeContext (dark/light, SSR-guarded)
  components/   → presentational React components (Layout, Hero, cards, grids)
  pages/        → Gatsby routes; compose components + ThemeProvider
    projects/   → filtered project listing pages
  images/       → static assets
```

Recommended build order: `types/` → `data/` → `styles/` → `context/` →
`components/` → `pages/`. Each subfolder `README.md` has the details.

## Conventions — do not violate

1. **Content lives in `data/`, never hard-coded in components.** Components are
   presentational and import typed data; editing copy must not require touching
   JSX.
2. **Types are the contract between `data/` and `components/`.** Shared shapes
   live in `src/types/`; don't duplicate or inline them.
3. **Guard browser-only APIs.** Gatsby renders on the server first. Accessing
   `window`, `document`, or `localStorage` outside `useEffect` will break the
   build — guard with `typeof window !== 'undefined'`.
4. **Styling goes through Tailwind + design tokens.** Use the semantic colors
   (`bg`, `ink`, `a1`–`a4`) wired to CSS variables in `tailwind.config.js`; do
   not hard-code hex values in components.
5. **Routing is file-based.** A page exists because a file exists in
   `src/pages/`. Don't invent a router.
6. **Flat URLs by default.** The site publishes at the domain root with an empty
   `pathPrefix`. Internal links use Gatsby `<Link>`; never hard-code absolute paths.
   Optional subpath deploys use `PATH_PREFIX` — see `src/pages/routing/README.md`.

## Environment

- Node 18+ (matches CI). `npm install` to set up.
- `npm run develop` for the dev server, `npm run typecheck` to run `tsc --noEmit`.
- **Never start the dev server yourself** — the user runs it.
- `npm run build:gh-pages` produces the production build for flat URLs;
  `npm run deploy` publishes to the `gh-pages` branch.

